        ]
      },
      "worked": "Adding the first two readings counts each adult once and the baby twice. Subtracting the adults’ combined mass leaves twice the baby’s mass.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Twice the baby's mass}&=(75+69-137)\\text{ kg}\\\\\\text{Twice the baby's mass}&=7\\text{ kg}\\\\\\text{Baby's mass}&=(7\\div2)\\text{ kg}\\\\\\text{Baby's mass}&=3.5\\text{ kg}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
